Z||000000||baldlobo||06-29-2001||01:55 PM||||let see it was starting off so good I got my reportcard(finally graduate from high school) when driving around with a friend then when back to school to drop him off.<BR>While, after he started to drive off he; I had thought of something to tell him so I try to catch up to him; I'm going 65 in a 60 trying to catch up to him, I look down at the gages for a second, then look back up and see this white van that was close in front of me.  I turn from the middle lane to the far left lane; that's when I felt the rear loosen so I corrected or overcorrected and spun out going across the other two lanes into the planter of one of my dads friends bisness. Completely f*cking up the front driverside fender, hood, box, taillight, headlight, grill, and rad. I don't have anything wrong with me.<BR>F*ck does this suck anyone in winnipeg, manitoba want to check out my handy work it's on notre dame right in front of the auto store inbetween wall St. and mcphilips St.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||06-29-2001||02:14 PM||||geeze! sorry to hear that! did something similar a few years back - going 40mph on a city street (40 zone) looked up and noticed a car slowing down in my lane just ahead, looked over my right shoulder to see if I can change lanes and when I look forward again the car had STOPPED!<P>  I was about halfway into the next lane already - if I had kept going I think i would of made it, but i instictively nailed the brakes, locking up all four tires, and the van slide straight forwards after that rearending the stopped car.<P>  Nobody was hurt in my wreck either, and I only bent my bumper a little and did about $1000 damage to the other car.<P>  Glad your ok - welcome to the bentmetal club - hope you get your wheels back together soon.<P>   Try not to beat yourself up for this too much - no matter how careful you are, sooner or later 1 out of 4 people that drive bang up a car pretty good - it happens. its normal. Cars are designed for it.||||reg||1
