Z||000018||Mach10||07-14-2001||02:25 PM||||The cops tagged you after the accident, and it's one of those 'summons' things? That's just a visit to the magistrate. Unless you blew a stop sign/are still on probabation, you probably won't get jack. I had one for driving with an expired license (long story, I thought I'd paid my renewal   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> ) Just go in, make up a good, sincere apology, and a credible explanation for the accident, plead guilty with just cause/not guilty and you'll only get stuck with the 30 "court" fee (It's a money-grabbing joke). Don't be rude, don't make stuff up. If you feel it wasn't your fault, say why, but keep it professional, and courteous.<P>*edit* spleling mistake<BR>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-14-2001).]<P>*edit* Oh, your best bet is that you lost control when avoiding a road hazard. Give them the same over-corrected schpeil you gave us. That should work. I just hope you're not on probation  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000019||baldlobo||07-14-2001||05:09 PM||||the accident happend about 10 days after I got my full drivers licence.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Mach10||07-14-2001||05:33 PM||||OH NO! That REALLY sucks. 10 days after your full license means that you are still on probation.<BR>This is what is going to happen. You will be cited, then charged, then Autopac will take you in for a "Show Cause" hearing. Then you are going to have your license suspended. I'm sorry man. I've been there, done that. Here's my advice: Go to one of those traffic ticket speciallists, and get some advice if you want to keep your license. Manitoba Driving laws are ****ing stupid. If you're lucky they will only suspend you for a months, if you don't get off. That REALLY sucks, man.<P>*edit* Unless you mean "10 days after I got off probation" in which case, you just have to swallow the demerits.<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||9
